      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Real-world impact</p>
      <h2 class="section-title mb-12">Sector scenarios & case studies</h2>
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A regional banking group operating across the Gulf Cooperation Council sought to modernize its cross-border trade-finance operations. Legacy correspondent banking relationships introduced multi-day settlement delays, reconciliation overhead, and exposure to documentation fraud. MEAICON deployed a permissioned blockchain ledger shared between the group's subsidiary banks, enabling letter-of-credit issuance and verification on a single trusted fabric. Smart contracts automated compliance checks against sanctions lists and KYC thresholds before any commitment was recorded, cutting settlement time from days to hours while producing an immutable audit trail for central bank examinations.</p>
          <p>In East Africa, a regional commercial bank faced escalating credential-phishing campaigns targeting retail and corporate customers. Attackers exploited mobile banking adoption growth and weak endpoint hygiene. MEAICON implemented a managed SOC with 24/7 threat detection, multi-factor authentication enforcement at all digital channels, and behavioral analytics that flagged session anomalies indicative of account takeover. The bank reduced fraud-related losses by over sixty percent within two quarters and satisfied central bank mandates for real-time incident reporting.</p>
          <p>Across North Africa, a Islamic finance institution needed to demonstrate Sharia-compliant transaction traceability to both auditors and its Sharia board. MEAICON architected a compliance-aware data pipeline that tagged every transaction with its underlying contract type, profit-sharing ratio, and asset-backing evidence, then surfaced this metadata through dashboards used by compliance, audit, and Sharia governance committees. This eliminated manual evidence-gathering cycles during quarterly reviews.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Case study highlight</h3>
